WEBVTT

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.670
Have him kill me.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.840
Have him kill me quickly.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.470
Hurt him a bit more first.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.350
It's your fault for trying to escape.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.980
No one's ever escaped from this place.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.130
Come back in your next life.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.900
When we lose one, another one comes.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.320
The fun never ends.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:21.280
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:32.630
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:44.390
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:50.690
The weak person I was is no more

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.280
I decided to just believe

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:03.410
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.250
I go towards you

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:14.960
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.090
I go towards you

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:23.140
Blown by the wind

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:28.600
Oh blown

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.480
Sleep Inside the Cage

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.220
You know what that means, Asian?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.970
"Be hopeful?"

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.220
Those are the words of the warden.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.520
The only people in here are those sentenced to life in prison or death, right?

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.600
What "hope" do we have?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.410
Enter.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.750
Prisoner number 579.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.750
Duke Tougou, a second-generation Japanese immigrant.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.420
Robbery.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.500
Rape.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.080
Arson.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.130
Attempted murder.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.000
Vandalism.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.670
Personality: Violent and cold.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.630
Sentence: Life in prison.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.140
Of course.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.650
I am the Warden, Kickers.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:02.440
579, there's something I want to tell you.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.650
Look at the inside yard.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.910
That's the prisoner check light.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.330
If anyone disappears, it turns red.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:18.170
You don't want to turn it red.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:25.380
The 19th man who turned it red just became a star on my pistol's grip.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.640
Make sure you don't become the 20th star.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.640
Nothing will ever happen between yesterday and tomorrow.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.350
Nothing will happen at all!

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.150
Nothing.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.360
Pound that into your head.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.860
Is that what you meant by "be hopeful?"

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:50.070
The psychology of the prisoners who come here exhibits a strange response.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.540
Tell them to die and they'll cling to life.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.870
Tell them to have hope, and they'll give up.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.920
I see.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.380
That sounds like the thoughts of a twisted little man.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:06.010
Say that again and I'll kill you on the spot!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.640
Take him away. Now!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.450
You've got a new friend!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.740
Get along!

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.380
Hey.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.710
How about you say hello at least, buddy?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.200
You don't need to give him any.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:16.620
Sit down, shut up, and watch everyone else eat.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.250
Hey, let me sit there.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.050
I'm Mouse.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.390
If you're not sure about something, just ask me.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:39.350
When I saw you come in, I figured we'd finally got somebody with some spine in here.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.640
I know what you're thinking.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.900
Join me and it'll happen.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.950
You shouldn't look at them too much.
They're the guys from the west special ward.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.870
Escape attempts, attacking guards, they'll do anything.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:09.840
Well, they don't know when God's going to call upon them, so it makes sense.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.170
Condemned prisoners?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.630
You got it.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.970
No talking!

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.970
Talking gets you put in solitary.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.980
What's with that attitude?

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.110
What about it, Bulldog?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.820
What?

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.700
Don't talk to me like that, Bulldog.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.620
Why you little-

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:44.870
Damn!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:08.730
You?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.730
Alaska Penal Code Article 350.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.240
A prisoner sentenced to life imprisonment

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:22.240
who attacks another person via a method that has the possibility to inflict lethal or great bodily harm...

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.580
is to be sentenced to death!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.840
You're new here,

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.590
so get on your knees and beg, and I'll forgive you.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.470
Get on your knees and lower your head.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:42.430
It won't help social morals if I beg.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:57.700
In accordance with Article 350, I'm transferring you to the west special ward for condemned prisoners!

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.600
Hey, 7.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.810
Can you hear me?

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.190
What?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.980
My name is Blue Eyes Zalas.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.240
Duke Tougou.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.360
You a jap?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.740
If you want something, spill it.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.780
Tell me one thing.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.660
What the hell were you doing back there?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.250
You weren't even remotely afraid of the death penalty.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.880
From the look of things, you were thinking "I'm leaving anyway," Tougou.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.880
So what?

00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:00.430
This is Pandora Island, they say it's impossible to escape.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:05.470
19 tried to escape and none survived.

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:09.770
I hear a few made it outside of the building, but it ended there.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:12.770
There's no way you could make it across those tides.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:15.900
The ones who died in the sea were lucky.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:19.110
Normally you're killed before you even make it that far.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:20.950
You saw it, didn't you?

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.280
With that light out there it's
impossible to make it to the roof.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.370
Some guys tried to go up the water spout,

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.720
but all of them were shot.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.390
Do you want to escape, Zalas?

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.100
So I was right?

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.850
You got a way out, Tougou?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.700
Hey, they're gone.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.540
Yeah.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:14.040
Floors five and six are factory areas, aren't they?

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:15.580
Yes.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.880
I work in the auto parts plant on the fifth floor.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.050
Get me the parts I'm about to tell you.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.550
Alright.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.920
Take off your socks.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.340
Now!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:05.720
Okay.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.620
I unthreaded the socks to make a thick thread, and rubbed it with Vaseline.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:39.460
I'll use a grinder and a file to whittle down metal into a thick thread.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:42.800
That'll finish the string file.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.970
And I've got the grease ready.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.470
OK, we'll do it tonight.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:17.160
Four people tried to escape by that water spout,

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.920
but they were all killed.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.000
What's your point?

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.510
You gonna try to escape?

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.390
I think you could do it.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.520
Would you take me too?

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.440
Break time is over.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.520
After inspection and roll call, return to your cells.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.480
I repeat:

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.070
Break time is over.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.610
After inspection and roll call, return to your cells.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.170
Yes, well done.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.170
OK.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:05.920
There's no time.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:06.960
Let's start.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.220
Alright.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:18.180
So there's really nobody out there planning something stupid?

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:19.890
Well?

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:27.690
Normally you would be in the west special ward.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.150
You've been sentenced to death, after all.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.740
You do know why I've made your sentence a life-sentence instead, right?

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.660
Of course.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.910
What about Tougou?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:42.120
Men like that will always try to run.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.710
No, for the moment he hasn't said a thing-

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.300
Don't miss it if he tries.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:51.380
If you do, you're going back to the west ward!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:17.550
Head along the building towards the water spout on the other side.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.390
Got it?

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:34.070
Once the next light passes, we'll go up this pipe.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.830
W-Will we really be OK even if the light shines on us?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.410
If you can keep up with me.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:49.960
It's coming.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:04.560
T-The light!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.600
Don't stop.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.060
Hurry.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.730
Here.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:22.080
Don't just stay there.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:23.740
Hurry, now.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.380
Why?

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:41.220
Why didn't they see us even with the light shining right on us?

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:42.760
Halation.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.350
Halation?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:47.430
What happens when the headlights of an oncoming car shine in your eyes?

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.690
Yes.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:53.860
Any objects inside the halation can't be seen by the source of the light.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.650
The area on the fifth floor is at just the right angle.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.280
That's why I went up that water spout.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.540
You're pretty damn good.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:10.330
Now then, let's go get wet.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.000
Take me too!

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.000
I won't slow you down!

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.710
So, please!

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:23.180
So I follow a rat, and look what I find!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:27.470
You fell for my trap.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.850
I thought you'd do it, Tougou.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:35.900
You're pretty damn good.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.360
I'll praise you for making it to the roof.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.360
You're star 20.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.000
Run!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:50.830
Dammit!

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.290
Quic-

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.350
Let's go.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:26.490
Now I know why I put grease all over my body.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.990
Now we won't get cold!

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:28.740
Don't talk.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.040
You'll waste energy.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.080
It's here.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.890
W-We did it!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.640
Take that, assholes!

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.500
You were going to escape from the start?

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.330
You've even got clothes prepared, damn you're good.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.670
Amazing.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.960
You even had a gun ready?

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:24.800
I see...

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:29.050
You're going to fight the jailers when they come after us, right?

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.980
Y-You can't-

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:49.870
Somebody said that they can't wait until your sentence comes up.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.000
D-Dammit.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:22:00.840
They thought I was going to talk before I died?

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:04.010
Tell me your name!

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:08.590
My name is...

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.010
Golgo 13.

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:13.770
I see.

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.480
You're...

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:16.520
Golgo?

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:49.550
Chiisana koto ni zenryoku ni naru kimi no sugata yuuki ni natta hibi

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:49.550
Those days I saw you giving your all for small things filled me with courage

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:57.020
Zutto horyuu shippanashi jya ugokenai

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:57.020
If I keep them suspended then I won't be able to move

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:06.570
GARASU no HAIWEI ni tatteiru you ni

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:06.570
It's like I'm standing on a glass highway

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:13.780
Yume to kiken to senaka awase demo

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:13.780
Even if I'm standing back to back with dreams and danger

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.920
Kono nagai michi wo sukoshizutsu arukou

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.920
I'll take this long road one step at a time

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:27.090
Soshite kimi wa ano koro mitai ni

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:27.090
And I need you to smile

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:30.090
Waratteite

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:30.090
Like you did back then

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:36.720
Shiokaze ni yurete sasayakiatta

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:36.720
It shook in the sea breeze and whispered

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:47.320
Kagayaiteita tooi ano hi wa kagerou

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:47.320
That distant and shining day is a shimmering haze

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:49.190
The shining days

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:55.160
Tsumaranai koto ni makeru ni wa hayasugiru

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:55.160
I can't lose to something so trivial

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:06.590
Golgo 13 takes out a drug kingpin who's being escorted by the FBI.

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:12.010
But a Mafia plot lurks beneath the surface.

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:15.510
What are they after?

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:20.270
Golgo will punish his employer's betrayal.

00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:22.230
Next time on Golgo 13:

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:26.900
The Target Who Came Back

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.520
The Target Who Came Back.

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:28.860
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
